\par\par \b \uc2 Tale Of Two G7s: As Europe Eyes  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 ,US Stresses Growth  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Brian Blackstone  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2004\par 17:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BOCA RATON, Fla. (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to dominate a weekend Group of Seven finance ministers' meeting, despite U.S. efforts to keep the focus on spurring growth in the global economy and the Middle East.  \par \par \uc2 Finance ministers from the world's largest economies are "going in the direction of clarification " of their previous statement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a European source said Saturday.  \par \par \uc2 "That's a good thing," the source said, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  discussions "advanced well" Friday.  \par \par \uc2 European finance ministers attending weekend G7 meetings have said they want the final communique summing up the meetings to include a reference to Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Is it necessary to change the Dubai communique?" Italian Finance Minister Guilio Tremonti asked earlier Saturday.  \par \par \uc2 "The Europeans presented the possibility to introduce something (in the communique) to increase the flexibility regarding Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said, referring to bilateral meetings between European ministers and John Snow, the U.S. Treasury secretary.  \par \par \uc2 The G7 communique is due for release later Saturday.  \par \par \uc2 The G7 comprises the U.S., Japan, Germany, France, the U.K., Italy and Canada. The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also takes part.  \par \par \uc2 In a statement following meetings in Dubai in September, the G7 said, "We emphasize that more flexibility in exchange rates is desirable for major countries or economic areas to promote smooth and widespread adjustments in the international financial system, based on market mechanisms."  \par \par \uc2 Investors took that as a green light to push the dollar lower. Yet massive Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has slowed the yen's climb against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , forcing the euro to bear much of the adjustment. The euro is now hovering near all-time highs against the dollar, which weighs on European exporters.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials have showed little inclination to alter their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the yen's rise totaled a record Y20 trillion last year.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo continued to heavily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets throughout January, buying dollars worth Y7 trillion - also a record volume for a single month.  \par \par \uc2 Japan Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said he conveyed to Snow that Tokyo maintains its view that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should move in a stable manner and that Tokyo is ready to "take appropriate steps against excessive moves" of the dollar against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Reflecting the apparent divergence in agendas between the U.S. and Europe, Snow said Saturday, "the focus on the conference, from my point of view, will continue to be growth and what we as ministers can do to build support for higher growth in our domestic economies of our countries and the economies of the developing world."  \par \par \uc2 "We have had a growth gap, a growth deficit, for some time, and the communique that came out of Dubai focused on the importance of growth and the things each of us can do in our own countries to encourage greater growth," he said.  \par \par \uc2 G7 leaders started meetings Saturday with a progress report on developments in Afghanistan and Iraq. The U.S. hopes to build support for increasing and speeding up financial aid to war-torn countries. Ministers also discussed ways to shut off terrorist financing.  \par \par \uc2 -By Brian Blackstone, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-741-4146; brian.blackstone@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 Takeshi Takeuchi also contributed to this article.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040207e0270004j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
