\par\par \b \uc2 WRAP: More Details On Japan's Heavy  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Intevention  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 647 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2004\par 05:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data released Friday shed more light on Tokyo's unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign to stop a sharp rise in the yen that could hurt exports.  \par \par \uc2 The ministry, in charge of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by its fastest pace ever in January due to massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , jumping $67.7 billion from a month earlier to $741.25 billion.  \par \par \uc2 That total marked another all-time high, and represented the fifth straight month of increases. As of November, the latest period when comparable international data are available, Japan held the biggest amount of foreign reserves for the 50th straight month, the ministry said.  \par \par \uc2 The data came out on the same day Japan's finance minister, Sadakazu Tanigaki, is scheduled to head to Boca Raton, Florida to face counterparts of the Group of Seven industrialized countries in a meeting that will run through Saturday.  \par \par \uc2 Some market participants expect Japan to face criticism from European officials at the meeting for its heavy interference in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the yen weak at a time when the dollar has been sliding fast against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 But Tanigaki indicated that Japan's aggressive efforts to curb a fast yen rise won't stop, and that he would make this clear to other finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors of the G7.  \par \par \uc2 "We've always said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should move stably in reflection of fundamentals, and if they move out of line with such fundamentals, we will take necessary action," he said at a news conference Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "Naturally, I will stress this at the G7."  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Only Dollars Bought In Fourth Quarter \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese officials have a good reason to fret about a further yen rise that could damage the economy's recovery: Tuesday, the dollar dropped to a near three-and-a-half-year low of Y105.22, and many \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders expect the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to fall further in weeks ahead. Around 0345 GMT, the dollar was at 106.06.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That perceived pressure on the dollar to fall against the yen, a result partly of market worries about the widening U.S. budget and current account deficits, is prompting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to push on with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  even if some trading partners appear to disapprove of the action.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had already last month announced that in January alone, the government had sold a staggering Y7.155 trillion in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a record amount for a single month. That came on top of a record Y20.057 trillion spent in 2003, far bigger than the previous record amount of Y7.64 trillion in 1999.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But ministry data released Friday gave more clues on how the government conducted its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - something that officials decline to discuss due to worries too much disclosure might make their action less effective.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data showed, for example, that all of the Y5.88 trillion \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spent in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the fourth quarter of 2003 was used to buy dollars, rather than euros.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 They also showed that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was carried out on 26 separate days during the three-month period, and that the biggest amount spent was on Dec. 10, when Y1.284 trillion was sold.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On that day, the dollar's exchange rate swung nearly two yen, moving between an intraday low of Y107.09 and high of Y108.72.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOF officials also said this week that the government paid banks a total of Y400 million in transaction fees for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets conducted in 2003 to prop up the dollar. That marks an increase of 150% in fee payments over the commissions to pay for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2002.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040206e0260003q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
