\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar lifted vs yen on jobs hopes but edgy pre-G7.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mariko Hayashibara  \par \uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2004\par 10:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 6 (Reuters) - The dollar rose to a one-week high on the yen on Friday after an upbeat comment on U.S. jobs from a Federal Reserve official, ahead of key employment data, but held steady on the euro in the wait for a G7 meeting later.  \par \par \uc2 Fed board governor Ben Bernanke, in comments on Thursday, said deflation fears had receded "very substantially" and that he was "pretty confident" the U.S. would see big numbers on jobs growth "pretty soon".  \par \par \uc2 Traders bought back the dollar on his comments after investors had been rattled by an unexpected rise in U.S. weekly jobless claims on Thursday, with the remarks raising speculation that U.S. interest rates might head higher sooner than thought.  \par \par \uc2 Monthly non-farm payrolls are due at 1330 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 "Bernanke did actually refer specifically to jobs, so (the dollar) is getting encouragement... Since we had such a bad number last month, we may see some positive figures today," said Chris Gothard, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Brown Brothers Harriman in London.  \par \par \uc2 "All this is a lot of positioning before the G7."  \par \par \uc2 At 0910 GMT, the dollar was trading at $1.2550 per euro, compared with $1.2539 in late New York, having hit a one-week low of $1.2636 in the previous session. Against the yen it was up nearly half a percent just below a one-week high of 106.46, a yen above a recent three-year low.  \par \par \uc2 US JOB DATA, G7  \par \par \uc2 Economists polled by Reuters expect 150,000 jobs were added to U.S. payrolls in January, up from a paltry 1,000 in December.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has been under pressure on the view that Group of Seven finance ministers meeting in Florida later in the day will do little to halt its slide and that the three main economic blocs, the U.S., the euro zone and Japan, do not hold a common position.  \par \par \uc2 Euro zone policy makers worry that euro strength could derail export-led economic recovery. The U.S. administration, on the other hand, has so far been content to see the dollar weaken as it boosts growth, not least in a presidential election year.  \par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , authorities have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in record amounts over the past year to ensure the yen does not appreciate too fast against the dollar and choke off an export led recovery.  \par \par \uc2 As a result, most analysts expect G7 finance ministers to deviate little from their last statement in Dubai in September, when they called for flexible exchange rates.  \par \par \uc2 "I see no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  slowing down (its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), and this is an interesting contrast from September," said Simon Derrick, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of New York in London.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow and Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki will hold a bilateral meeting 0230 GMT on Saturday.  \par \par \uc2 Shortly before his departure for the meeting, Tanigaki said he would tell his G7 counterparts that Japan will take action against irregular movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 In Europe, Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered its key interest rates by a quarter of a percentage point to 2.5 percent, their lowest level since 1945.  \par \par \uc2 The Swedish crown rose against the euro and the dollar as accompanying comments from the bank indicated it was less biased towards lower rates than investors had expected.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040206e026001ck\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
