\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Jan Foreign Reserves $741.25B; Up $67.7B On Month  \b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2004\par 00:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose $67.7 billion in January from a month earlier to $741.25 billion, the Finance Ministry said Friday.  \par \par \uc2 January was the fifth straight month of increase and marked another record high for the reserves, highlighting the massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities in January aimed at preventing the yen's rise from hurting the nation's export-led recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's reserves of convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gold and International Monetary Fund special drawing rights in January were up from $673.53 billion in December, the ministry said.  \par \par \uc2 December's amount was up $28.96 billion from November.  \par \par \uc2 The $67.7 billion increase, which was the biggest single-month growth on record, was largely due to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a Finance Ministry official briefing reporters said.  \par \par \uc2 According to earlier-released data, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  ordered the Bank of Japan to sell Y7.15 trillion in January. That came on top of a record Y20.057 trillion spent in 2003, far bigger than the last record amount of Y7.64 trillion in 1999.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo may be criticized for the huge \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amount when finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  heads of the Group of Seven leading industrial nations get together in Boca Raton, Florida, for a two-day meeting that kicks off later Friday.  \par \par \uc2 According to ministry data, the dollar's high for the month was Y108.30, hit on Jan. 9, while the low was Y105.23 on Jan. 28. The euro's high was $1.2790 on Jan. 14, while its low was $1.2347 on Jan. 20.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's foreign reserves were the largest in the world for the 50th consecutive month as of November, the latest month for which comparable data from most other nations are available, the ministry said.  \par \par \uc2 Japan had $636.0 billion in reserves, followed in second place by China with $406.9 billion, although the figures for China are for October. The euro zone was third with $248.0 billion, Taiwan was fourth with $203.5 billion, while South Korea came fifth with $150.2 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Japan typically invests much of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  it acquires via market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in U.S. Treasurys and European government bonds.  \par \par \uc2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by John Gibson and Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 4146  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040205e025000y9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
