\par\par \b \uc2 Asia ForexUS Likely Benign At G7 On  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2004\par 08:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 For all the benefits from a falling dollar, the U.S. can't say its policy has shifted to a weak dollar, Fink said. "If the U.S. government publicly announces a weak-dollar policy, the greenback would likely nosedive" and may prompt foreigners to unload U.S. bonds, Fink said.  \par \par \uc2 And if long-term interest rates rise as a result, stocks may fall, the U.S. economy may slow, and its government will face larger interest payments on its growing budget deficit.  \par \par \uc2 That's one reason the U.S. at the G7 meeting won't likely harangue \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  about its dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is using to help finance the U.S. budget deficit by purchasing U.S. Treasurys, Fink said.  \par \par \uc2 Despite what seems to be U.S. tolerance, some players said Japan will likely stick to just slowing the dollar's fall against the yen for a while - action it calls "smoothing."  \par \par \uc2 Japanese exporters are said to have already sold most of their February and March receipts through forward agreements, NLI's Kumagai said. MOF officials probably know it and may not see the need of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the dollar sharply higher - especially before meeting their European peers - he said.  \par \par \uc2 Exporters didn't sell around Y105.44 Thursday, traders said, though some of them have reportedly set their in-house exchange rates near Y105.00.  \par \par \uc2 "Offers from exporters are thick above the current (dollar/yen) level, but they aren't coming down," said Tatsuro Karitani, vice president of Mizuho Corporate Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  division.  \par \par \uc2 Exporters appear active in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options market instead, where demand for yen call/dollar put options has continued to rise before the G7 meeting.  \par \par \uc2 Demand for risk-reversal positions - where a hedger sells dollar call/yen put options and use the premiums to buy dollar put/yen call options - has been firm, as exporters and corporations increasingly see a weaker dollar ahead, options traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "Buying interest for yen calls show no signs of weakening at all," an options broker said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040205e0250007o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
