\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW: Japan To Skirt G7 Criticism -Ex-BOJ Wakatsuki  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 748 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2004\par 08:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's Group of Seven partners are unlikely to criticize Tokyo's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite Europe's unhappiness about it, because the U.S. tolerates the policy, a former senior Bank of Japan official said.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is speculating that European nations will surely criticize \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  so heavily in the market and will ask Tokyo to share more of the burden of the dollar's underlying weakness," said Mikio Wakatsuki, who was formerly an executive director at the BOJ.  \par \par \uc2 "But Japan won't get into much trouble at the meeting because the U.S. has no problem with Tokyo's huge yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said Wednesday in an interview with Dow Jones Newswires.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record Y20 trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the yen's rise against the dollar, and sold another whopping Y7 trillion in January. Despite that effort, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen roughly 12% against the yen since last August and now flirts with three year and five month-lows just above Y105.  \par \par \uc2 Some European countries, worried that the euro's ascent against the dollar could hurt their economies, seem unhappy that Japan is spending so much to prevent the yen from rising too much against the dollar, Wakatsuki said.  \par \par \uc2 But the United States doesn't seem to mind since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helps prevent the dollar from entering free fall, a situation that could disturb U.S. financial markets.  \par \par \uc2 Wakatsuki said he expects few surprises to come out of the meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors of the G7 industrialized countries in Boca Raton, Florida.  \par \par \uc2 That's because the finance officials are unlikely to agree on making any drastic changes in the section of their joint communique that deals with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Wakatsuki, who is currently senior fellow at private think tank Japan Research Institute.  \par \par \uc2 "Besides, it's extremely unlikely the G7 communique will mention anything about a particular \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The market is rife with speculation on how the G7 nations will address the current weak-dollar trend. In particular, attention is focused on whether the communique's section on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have different wording from that of the previous meeting in Dubai, where the G7 called for "more flexibility" in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.  \par \par \uc2 The phrase jolted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as traders interpreted it as a veiled criticism of Japan's and other Asian governments' aggressive interference in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    No Strong Dollar Message Likely \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market players now believe the G7 nations won't send a strong message against the dollar's weakness at the meeting because Washington seems happy with a gradual dollar decline. Traders say the greenback has become weak enough to keep U.S. manufacturers content in an election year but is falling at a slow enough pace so as not to cause turmoil in financial markets.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The dollar's decline has been orderly so far, so there's absolutely no need for the U.S. to fret about exchange rates," Wakatsuki said, noting that Washington will instead try to steer the focus of G7 talks to expanding global economic growth.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ's recent decision to ease its monetary policy settings could help Japan counter any criticism that it's relying too much on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support its fragile economic recovery, Wakatsuki said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could argue that its economy is still weak and warrants yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but also that it's doing more than just selling yen to stimulate growth," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier in the month, the BOJ eased monetary policy by boosting its liquidity target by Y3 trillion to a new range of Y30 trillion to Y35 trillion, in a surprise move.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Whatever the outcome of the G7 meeting, Wakatsuki expects the current weak-dollar trend to remain intact for some time on lingering wariness over the U.S. "twin" fiscal and trade deficits.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar will also come under downward pressure from any yen-bullish factors, such as non-Japanese investors' strong appetite for Japanese stocks or prospects for steady growth in the Japanese economy, Wakatsuki said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't be any good in turning this trend around because speculators will just take advantage of MOF action," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040205e0250007n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
