\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  in 4th qtr - NY Fed.  \b0\par\par\uc2 471 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2004\par 22:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NEW YORK, Feb 5 (Reuters) - U.S. monetary authorities did\par not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets on their own\par behalf during the October-December quarter, the Federal Reserve\par Bank of New York said on Thursday.\par     However, the quarterly report noted that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has publicly confirmed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the fact,\par including the MOF's announcement that it sold 1.5996 trillion\par yen between Oct. 30 and Nov. 26, and another 2.2519 trillion\par yen between Nov. 27 and Dec. 26.\par  \par     During the three months to Dec. 31, the dollar depreciated\par 3.8 percent against the yen and 7.5 percent against the euro.\par     "Although ... data releases provided evidence of ongoing\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economic recovery, concerns regarding the size of the current  \f28 \par \par \uc2 account deficit and expectations for U.S. interest rates to  \par \par \uc2 remain low weighed on the dollar," the New York Fed said.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The U.S. monetary authorities did not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market during the quarter," it added.\par     The report also took note of investors' wariness about\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It said investors were more reluctant to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weaken the dollar against the yen than the euro, because  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 concerns of Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remain elevated.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Market participants reportedly felt more comfortable  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expressing negative dollar views against the euro and other  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 higher-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as they remained highly attuned to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 official views on recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Many noted that while Asian officials consistently  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expressed discomfort with their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' appreciation, there  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 was less certainty about the views of European officials on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 policy implications of a strong euro," the New York Fed said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More recently, European officials have said the dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 needs to strengthen to prevent a crisis, but not at their  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expense or too rapidly. European officials have also expressed  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 discomfort towards Asian countries that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep their  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weaker than the dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Fed report also said contrasting expectations for  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 monetary policy between the U.S. and other economies  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 contributed to the appreciation of several other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 against the dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Over the quarter, the British pound rose 7.5 percent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the dollar and the Australian dollar surged 10.6  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent against the U.S. dollar, as those countries' central  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 banks began to raise interest rates.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At the end of December, the value of euro and yen reserve  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 holdings totaled about $19.9 billion for the Federal  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve's System Open Market Account and about $19.9 billion  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for the Treasury's Exchange Stabilization Fund.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Details are as follows:\par     FOREIGN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  HOLDINGS OF U.S. MONETARY AUTHORITIES\par     Balance on Dec. 31, 2003:\par     FEDERAL RESERVE SYSTEM OPEN MARKET ACCOUNT:\par     Euro   $11.052 billion\par     Yen     $8.816 billion\par     Total  $19.868 billion\par     U.S. TREASURY EXCHANGE STABILIZATION FUND:\par     Euro   $11.037 billion\par     Yen     $8.816 billion\par     Total  $19.854 billion.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040205e0250035y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
