\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro up vs dlr as ECB holds rates, Trichet focus.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Burton Frierson  \par \uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2004\par 14:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 5 (Reuters) - The euro drifted up against the dollar on Thursday after a widely expected European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision to leave rates unchanged, while markets also waited for ECB chief Jean-Claude Trichet to be quizzed on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Analysts had predicted that budding euro zone recovery and tame inflation would trump concerns about the euro's rapid rise to record highs versus the dollar in January in the central bankers' rate decision, which kept rates at 2.0 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Exchange rates should still figure prominently into Trichet's 1330 GMT news conference, especially with the dollar's decline likely to force its way onto the agenda of Friday's meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers and central bankers.  \par \par \uc2 "The market wants to know if they (the ECB) have an opinion on the euro right now because it is the day before the G7," said Peter Fontaine, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at KBC in Brussels.  \par \par \uc2 "We would like to hear some kind of pre-positioning going into tomorrow's G7. If they don't it's like saying 'let the euro rise further'."  \par \par \uc2 By 1300 GMT the euro was up more than a third of percent at $1.2584, some three cents below the record highs it hit in January.  \par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also gained more than a third of a percent against the yen to 132.70 yen, while the dollar held steady against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 105.45 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Though not far from recent three-year lows against the yen, markets have been cautious about pushing it much lower due to worries monetary authorities in Tokyo might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb any export-harming yen strength.  \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, sterling trimmed its losses against the euro and gained versus the dollar after the Bank of England raised interest rates a quarter point, as widely expected, and issued a hawkish accompanying statement.  \par \par \uc2 Economists expect U.S. initial jobless claims to show a median total of 340,000 new filings when figures are announced at 1330 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 TRICHET AWAITED  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have been roiled by comments in recent weeks, primarily from European policymakers, expressing concern over the dollar's descent. This is likely to make journalists eager to press Trichet on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But dealers are leaning toward the view there is little Trichet can say to undermine the euro's strength since most see the likelihood of the G7 coming to the dollar's rescue at the weekend as remote at best.  \par \par \uc2 "(At the G7) we do not expect the U.S. to acquiesce to demands from Asia or Europe to try to prevent further dollar weakness. There is still nothing in it for the U.S. in pushing for that," said Shahab Jalinoos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) left rates steady but BOJ Governor Toshihiko Fukui repeated his concerns about the strong yen.  \par \par \uc2 Fukui said early on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must carefully watch the impact of the yen's recent strength, saying the stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not problematic in the long term but it could pose problems in the short term.  \par \par \uc2 The G7 called in September for more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility, a call markets interpreted as aimed at Asian nations including Japan. Since then, however, Japan has loudly protested against yen strength and is not expected to ease off yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say this has left European officials frustrated as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was one factor driving up the euro against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 However, many think Washington is happy with a weaker dollar as it helps problems of disinflation and the current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 Seeing such differences, analysts expect G7 ministers will not vary their reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  significantly from the wording of the September communique.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040205e02500266\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
