\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro gains vs dollar ahead of ECB, Trichet.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Burton Frierson  \par \uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2004\par 11:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 5 (Reuters) - The euro drifted higher against the dollar on Thursday ahead of a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting expected to keep interest rates on hold and seen unlikely to raise any fresh concerns about the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts expect budding euro zone recovery and tame inflation to trump concerns about the euro's rapid rise to record highs versus the dollar in January in the central bankers' rate decision, which is due at 1245 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Markets are therefore focused on ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet's 1330 GMT news conference and the possibility he will comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves ahead of Friday's meeting of Group of Seven (G7) finance ministers and central banks.  \par \par \uc2 But dealers are leaning toward the view there is little at this point that Trichet can say to undermine the euro's advance since most see the likelihood of the G7 coming to the dollar's rescue at the weekend as remote at best.  \par \par \uc2 "No one is expecting an ECB rate move. As far as \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  go they may signal that they do not like excessive volatility - that is not new information," said Shahab Jalinoos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \par \par \uc2 "(At the G7) we do not expect the U.S. to acquiesce to demands from Asia or Europe to try to prevent further dollar weakness. There is still nothing in it for the U.S. in pushing for that."  \par \par \uc2 By 1035 GMT the euro was up a third of percent at $1.2576, some three cents below the record highs it hit in January.  \par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also gained a third of a percent against the yen to 132.63 yen, while the dollar held steady against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 105.45 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Though not far from recent three-year lows against the yen, markets have been cautious about pushing it much lower due to worries monetary authorities in Tokyo might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb any export-harming yen strength.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of England is also meeting and expected to announce at 1200 GMT a quarter-point rise in UK borrowing costs to bring official interest rates to 4.0 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was a quarter percent lower against the broadly firmer euro but a touch higher against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 TRICHET AWAITED  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have been roiled by comments in recent weeks, primarily from European policymakers, expressing concern over the dollar's descent, which is also expected force its way onto the G7's agenda.  \par \par \uc2 "At today's ECB meeting the main focus will be on the press conference and what they think about the euro developments ahead of the G7," said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research Credit Agricole Indosuez.  \par \par \uc2 "If anything the ECB will probably play down any concern about euro strength, which suggests that the risks will continue to be for a higher euro."  \par \par \uc2 Prior to the European rate announcements, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) left rates steady but BOJ Governor Toshihiko Fukui repeated his concerns about the strong yen.  \par \par \uc2 Fukui said early on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must carefully watch the impact of the yen's recent strength, saying the stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not problematic in the long term but it could pose problems in the short term.  \par \par \uc2 The G7 called in September for more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility, a call markets interpreted as aimed at Asian nations including Japan. Since then, however, Japan has loudly protested against yen strength and is not expected to ease off yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say this has left European officials frustrated as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was one factor driving up the euro against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 However, many think Washington is happy with a weaker dollar as it helps problems of disinflation and the current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 Seeing such differences, analysts expect G7 ministers will not vary their reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  significantly from the wording of the September communique.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040205e025001ln\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
