\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro steady before ECB, Trichet awaited.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mariko Hayashibara  \par \uc2 618 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2004\par 10:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 5 (Reuters) - The euro was steady against the dollar on Thursday ahead of a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting expected to leave interest rates on hold but provide President Jean-Claude Trichet with a chance to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.   \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect healthy euro zone recovery and tame inflation to trump concerns about the euro's rapid rise to record highs versus the dollar in January in the central bankers' rate decision, which is due at 1245 GMT.   \par \par \uc2  But analysts said with the focus on an imminent Group of Seven (G7) meeting and key U.S. job data on Friday, the market was expected to show only a subdued reaction to a batch of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meetings, including one at the Bank of England (BoE).   \par \par \uc2  "I don't think people want to do an awful lot now. They just want to wait until the G7 is out of the way," said Ian Gunner at Mellon Bank.   \par \par \uc2  At 0855 GMT the euro was flat on the day at $1.2545.   \par \par \uc2  TRICHET AWAITED   \par \par \uc2  Trichet's 1330 GMT news conference gives journalists an opportunity to quiz him ahead of Friday's meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers and central bankers at which the dollar's decline is expected to be on the agenda.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have been roiled by comments in recent weeks, primarily from European policymakers, expressing concern over the dollar's descent.   \par \par \uc2  "At today's ECB meeting the main focus will be on the press conference and what they think about the euro developments ahead of the G7," said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research Credit Agricole Indosuez.   \par \par \uc2  "If anything the ECB will probably play down any concern about euro strength, which suggests that the risks will continue to be for a higher euro."   \par \par \uc2  In Britain, the BoE is expected to announce at 1200 GMT a quarter-point rise in UK borrowing costs to bring official interest rates to 4.0 percent.   \par \par \uc2  G7 STILL FOCUS   \par \par \uc2  The dollar was steady against the yen at 105.45 yen. It is not far from recent three-year lows against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but markets have been cautious to push it much lower due to worries monetary authorities in Tokyo might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Prior to the European rate announcements, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) left rates steady, but BOJ Governor Toshihiko Fukui repeated his concerns about the strong yen.   \par \par \uc2  Fukui said early on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must carefully watch the impact of the yen's recent strength, saying the stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not problematic in the long term but it could pose problems in the short term.   \par \par \uc2  Fukui also said that in general an easier monetary policy indirectly resulted in a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The G7 called in September for more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility, a call markets interpreted as aimed at Asian nations including Japan. Since then, however, Japan has loudly protested against export-damaging yen strength and is not expected to ease off yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Analysts say this has left European officials frustrated as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was one factor driving up the euro sharply higher against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  However, many think Washington is happy with a weaker dollar as it helps problems of disinflation and the current account deficit.   \par \par \uc2  Seeing such differences, analysts expect G7 ministers will not vary their reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  significantly from the wording of the September communique.   \par \par \uc2  The market focus was on whether the statement would refer to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability.   \par \par \uc2  Traders were also cautious ahead of a key U.S. jobs report on Friday as an improving labour market could hold the key to the timing of a rate hike in the United States.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040205e025001eq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
