\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Mizoguchi -  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market wrong to focus on US deficits.  \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2004\par 02:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 5 (Reuters) - The U.S. economy remains strong and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets should not simply focus on bad points such as the budget and trade deficits, Japan's top financial diplomat said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "We believe the U.S. economic base is fundamentally strong," Zembei Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters at the ministry.  \par \par \uc2 "Markets have got into a habit of focusing on the bad points such as the twin deficits. It is wrong to overstress these points."  \par \par \uc2 Japan, concerned about the damage a strong yen does to exports, which are leading its economic recovery, has taken aim at what it sees as speculative moves to push the dollar down, repeatedly stressing the strength of the U.S. economy.  \par \par \uc2 It poured some 20 trillion yen ($190 billion) into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last year to curb the yen's rise against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and another seven trillion yen last month alone.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading around 105.50 yen on Thursday. It had fallen to around 105.20 yen on Tuesday, its lowest in nearly 3-= years. It also hit record lows against the euro last month.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts expect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come under scrutiny at this weekend's meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs in Florida, though Mizoguchi, who will attend the meeting, sought to play down the possibility of conflict.  \par \par \uc2 "Rather than making demands of each other, everyone will stress the efforts they are making to help the global recovery," he said, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability would be one factor in this.  \par \par \uc2 But \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against excessive volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates when necessary, he said, adding that he believed that markets will realise the medium-term strength and stability of the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040205e0250009j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
