\par\par \b \uc2 Yen seen rising towards 100 per dollar.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Justyna Pawlak  \par \uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2004\par 13:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 4 (Reuters) - The yen will continue forcing itself free from caps set by official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming year and rise further from recent three-year highs against the dollar, a Reuters survey showed on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Within the next 12 months, foreign investors' appetite for Japanese stocks, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows from exports and a persistent weakness of the U.S. dollar will probably push the yen towards the psychological level of 100 yen per greenback, a rate not seen since November 1995, according to the monthly poll.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the upward pressure on the yen to encounter little resistance from the world's top economic powers, with the Group of Seven (G7) industrialised nations seen unable to cobble together a common policy to put a floor under the feeble dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The G7 will hold a closely-watched meeting this Friday and Saturday in Florida. But it should have little bearing on the yen's rally even if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rates and the dollar's weakness dominate discussions, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 "While \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to continue heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the foreseeable future, the psychological 100 yen level will eventually have to give way as fundamentals argue for further yen strength," said Michael Woolfolk, Bank of New York analyst in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The median forecast from 50 analysts, polled between February 2 and 4, showed the dollar/yen exchange rate at 105.00 in one month, from Tuesday's three-year low of 105.20.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar is seen fetching 104.00 yen in three months, 103.00 in half a year and 100.00 in 12 months' time.  \par \par \uc2 These forecasts show analysts slightly more bullish on the yen now than they were a month ago when the three-, six-and 12-month median predictions stood at 105.00, 104.00 and 102.00 yen, respectively.  \par \par \uc2 JAPAN FLEXES \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  MUSCLES  \par \par \uc2 Japan spent more than 20 trillion yen ($190 billion) to keep the yen's gains versus the dollar in check through official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, and more than seven trillion yen in January alone.  \par \par \uc2 This massive selling of yen was driven by concern that Japan's fragile economic recovery could fail if a strong yen eats into exports, the main driver of Japanese growth.  \par \par \uc2 Senior Japanese government adviser Haruhiko Kuroda reiterated these worries on Wednesday, saying in an interview with Reuters:  \par \par \uc2 "It is truly amazing how the United States is propelling the global economy. Japan is almost half as big, and it would be bad for the global economy if it were to slip back into recession ... because of a higher yen."  \par \par \uc2 Washington is not expected to agree to any joint measures aimed at supporting the dollar during talks at the Florida G7 meeting.  \par \par \uc2 And Europe is seen piling more criticism on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own, which limits the yen's gains and transfers some of the dollar's weakness onto the euro.  \par \par \uc2 But Japan is still expected to continue throwing more yen on to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in a bid to at least smooth its rise. Meanwhile investors are widely expected to resist the officials.  \par \par \uc2 "Post-G7, we see the (Japanese) \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  prepared to let dollar/yen slip below 105," said Peter Luxton, analyst at Informa Global Markets in London.  \par \par \uc2 "But 100 is a big number, and it will be stoutly defended ahead of this critical level."  \par \par \uc2 One \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair which investors will be watching after this week's G7 meeting is euro/yen. They will be waiting to see if there is any impact of Europe's demands that Japan and other Asian nations share some of the burden of a weak dollar by letting their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise more on the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 This month's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll put the median euro/yen forecast at 132.93 in one month, 133.90 in three-and six-months and at 131.10 in one year. On Wednesday, euro/yen traded at 132.20.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040204e024001xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
