\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ Watch: Steady Policy This Wk But Easing Bias Remains  \b0\par\par\uc2 802 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2004\par 09:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Hiroshi Inoue \par  \par    A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Bank of Japan board members will likely leave monetary policy settings unchanged at their meeting this week, though they'll keep their finger on the trigger ready to ease more if needed.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The direction of the yen and stock prices in the run-up to Japan's fiscal year-end on March 31 is key in determining whether the BOJ takes further near-term action.  \par \par \uc2 Signaling it is willing to loosen its already ultra-easy policy despite a continuing economic recovery in Japan, the BOJ surprised financial markets last month by raising its liquidity target.  \par \par \uc2 People close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  say the board may consider a further loosening as there is no sign deflation will end soon, and the yen's appreciation against the dollar threatens to undermine the economy's recovery, which has been driven by a sharp rise in exports.  \par \par \uc2 "Volatility in financial markets, especially in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , before the end of March remains a big concern" for the BOJ, said a person close to the BOJ.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a fresh three-and-a-half-year low of Y105.47 in New York trading on Jan. 27. At 0825 GMT, the dollar was quoted around Y105.65.  \par \par \uc2 Easing action is therefore possible at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's board meeting scheduled for March 15-16 following steady policy decisions at meetings this week and on Feb. 26.  \par \par \uc2 Financial market participants too expect the BOJ to stand pat on Wednesday and Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "Additional monetary easing is still possible until Japan overcomes deflation, although the economy is recovering," said Eiji Dohke, chief strategist at UBS Securities, "But only two weeks have passed since the latest easing, so a policy shift this week is unlikely."  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Strong Yen Worries \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 On Jan. 20, seven of the nine board members voted to raise the BOJ's liquidity target by Y3 trillion to a range of Y30 trillion to Y35 trillion.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ said then that the easing was to maintain the economy's recovery, although financial market participants mostly interpreted the move as squarely aimed at helping the government fight further appreciation of the yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Since then, people close to the BOJ have said the decision to ease was not only based on economic factors, but also on political considerations and international relations.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 They say BOJ Governor Toshihiko Fukui hoped the easing move would deflect any criticism at a meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers and central bankers in Florida Friday and Saturday that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  too much in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets and should take other action to boost its economy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen will still likely be a focus for BOJ policy making after the G7 meeting.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is a worry," BOJ Deputy Governor Toshiro Mutoh said Friday. "We must keep a close eye on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market going forward."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 According to another person close to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Fukui is keen to act quickly on any sign of financial market instability before the end of March.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If the yen's rise accelerated, this would worsen corporate sentiment and reverse the uptrend of stock prices," the source said. "Such moves would be a big problem for the economy and private firms before March" and could lead the BOJ to further increase its liquidity target.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fukui told Japan's Parliament last week that the BOJ wants to keep short- and long-term interest rates "as low as possible" so that companies can cheaply procure funds for investment.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Keeping interest rates low should also make the yen relatively unattractive compared with other countries, meaning less money pouring into Japan and strengthening the yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, any further policy action may encounter some opposition on the board.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Board member Teizo Taya last week indicated that he was one of two who voted against the latest easing, saying it isn't clear that increases in liquidity boost the impact of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's ultra-easy policy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Views are split on whether an increase in the account balance target would strengthen the policy duration effect...but I personally think it is doubtful," Taya said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speculation within the BOJ is that Miyako Suda was the other board member against the latest easing.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ will make public the names of the two dissenters when it issues minutes from last month's policy meeting on March 2.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taya, Suda and Kazuo Ueda voted against the previous easing last October.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Hiroshi Inoue, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-9203; hiroshi.inoue@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Hiroshi Inoue, a correspondent for Dow Jones Newswires in Tokyo, has covered the Bank of Japan for a dozen years and also looks at credit markets.)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hugh Lawson  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1042 4131  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040202e022000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
