\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Slips Vs Yen But Japan MOF Bids Support  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 779 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2004\par 06:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar ticked lower against the yen in Asia Monday on familiar factors, such as concerns about the U.S.'s twin deficits, but it remained above the three-and-a-half-year low it set last week thanks to suspected bids from the Japanese monetary authorities.  \par \par \uc2 After touching an intraday high of Y105.78, the greenback edged down and remained caught in an extremely tight band in the mid-Y105s, as players were unwilling to take on fresh positions ahead of the two-day meeting of Group of Seven finance officials from Friday in Boca Raton, Florida.  \par \par \uc2 Traders suspected Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  was placing covert bids to prevent the greenback from tumbling below its low of Y105.47 set last Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Some players said Japanese banks often associated with the MOF's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were steadily absorbing dollar offers, helping the U.S. unit remain above Y105.60.  \par \par \uc2 Ryohei Muramatsu, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade at Commerzbank's Tokyo branch, warned that Y105.60 was a key chart point for the dollar in the near term.  \par \par \uc2 "If the dollar fails to sustain this level, it may easily tumble below Y105," he said. "The MOF is aware of this, so it might be thinking of conducting yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in significant amounts to defend this level."  \par \par \uc2 But Muramatsu expects overall dollar-bearish sentiment to remain intact since factors that have been weighing on the greenback, such as the huge U.S. trade deficit and terrorism concerns, haven't gone away. Weaker-than-expected U.S. fourth quarter GDP data joined that list late last week.  \par \par \uc2 Data released Friday showed the Bank of Japan, acting on behalf of the MOF, spent a record Y7.15 trillion in January to keep the yen from appreciating rapidly and threatening the country's export-led recovery. That's more than a third of the Y20.1 trillion the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  during all of 2003.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y105.64, below Y105.76 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at Y105.93 late Friday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2458, lower than $1.2474 late Friday in New York. The euro was at $1.2414 in Tokyo Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y131.61, down from Y131.95 in New York late Friday. The euro was at Y131.50 in Tokyo late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8249, a tad up from $1.8246 in New York and higher than $1.8163 in Tokyo Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro drifted lower against the yen on speculation that European nations may ask Japan to shoulder a heavier burden of the dollar's weakness at the G7 meeting, making it harder for Tokyo to act against the yen's sharp rise.  \par \par \uc2 The unwinding of euro/yen long positions kept the euro on a weak note against the dollar as well, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 A slew of pre-G7 speculation may cause choppy moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets this week, but few market players expect any big surprises from the G7 meeting itself.  \par \par \uc2 The joint communique due out after the meeting won't be much different from that of the previous meeting in Dubai, which called for "flexibility" in exchange rates, said Masamichi Koike, head of spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking.  \par \par \uc2 "There's not much reason to change the communique's wording, since the United States is happy with the dollar's current downtrend and the euro has calmed after its fast-pitched rise," Koike said.  \par \par \uc2 Japan may certainly face criticism for its aggressive yen-selling campaign, but traders expect that to only happen behind the scenes.  \par \par \uc2 "It's true European countries are unhappy with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a European bank trader said.  \par \par \uc2 "But what can \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  do to prop up its economy besides weakening the yen, given that the nation's monetary conditions are already ultra-easy? No one can criticize Japan for trying to stem deflation by avoiding a further strengthening of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040202e02200047\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
