\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar holds near 3-yr low vs yen, G7 looms.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Justyna Pawlak  \par \uc2 723 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2004\par 10:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 2 (Reuters) - The dollar held just above a recent three-year low against the yen on Monday with the market wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BoJ) after suspected action by it earlier in the session. The spectre of a key meeting by the Group of Seven (G7) industrialised nations later this week hung over the market, with investors unwilling to take major positions until they know how the G7 will react to the persistent weakness of the dollar. The dollar has won some ground against the euro in the run-up to the closely-watching meeting in Florida this Friday and Saturday, and analysts widely expect it to trade in narrow ranges in the final days.  \par \par \uc2 "The G7 will be the main issue throughout this week," said Ian Gunner, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Mellon Bank in London.  \par \par \uc2 "The key question is whether the United States will agree to put its name to a statement that will have words like 'excessive movements are undesirable'," he said. At 0905 GMT, the dollar traded unchanged on the day against the euro at $1.2475 and the yen at 105.65.  \par \par \uc2 Many traders suspected the BoJ, which spent a record 7.15 trillion yen ($67.2 billion) to prop up the dollar in January, was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on Monday in the 105.60 yen area. The BoJ acts on behalf of Japan's finance ministry.  \par \par \uc2 "It seems that the MOF (\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 105.58 yen," said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was little moved by news that the euro zone manufacturing sector grew a little faster in January.  \par \par \uc2 The Reuters Eurozone Purchasing Managers' Index rose to 52.5 from 52.4 in December. Analysts had forecast the index at 52.9.  \par \par \uc2 WORLD'S FINANCE CHIEFS MEET  \par \par \uc2 Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks by various European officials worried that a stronger euro could damage Europe's fragile economic recovery has slowed the dollar's slide.  \par \par \uc2 Now with the Florida meeting imminent, one growing view is it is likely to end without agreement on any strong statement aimed at halting the dollar's decline, which has in part been driven by the size of the U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 International Monetary Fund Managing Director Horst Koehler said on Monday a credible global strategy was needed to avoid pressuring any major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  area.  \par \par \uc2 He added that while a strong euro and weaker dollar was facilitating current account rebalancing he shared euro zone officials' sentiment that the situation needed monitoring.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the U.S. authorities appeared in no hurry to warn against the greenback's weakness, as the U.S. economy was benefiting from the cheaper dollar while U.S. shares have rallied recently, unscathed by the dwindling value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But others said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could come under fire, particularly from European countries.  \par \par \uc2 "There are voices in Europe that say Japan and other Asian countries should shoulder more of the burden of the dollar's adjustment," said Daisuke Uno, market analyst at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp.  \par \par \uc2 At its last meeting, in Dubai, the G7 called for flexible exchange rates, which markets read as criticism of Asian nations for keeping the dollar underpinned to help their own export competitiveness. The September statement from Dubai sent the dollar reeling.  \par \par \uc2 More U.S. manufacturing data is due later in the day, with the Institute of Supply Management's index seen rising to 64.0 in January from December's 63.4.  \par \par \uc2 "The ISM could generate some impact at the margin. Given that everyone is looking at the U.S. labour market, the employment component will be looked at," said Mellon Bank's Gunner.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. President George W. Bush is also due to propose his election-year budget plan on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The $2.4 trillion budget is expected to cut dozens of government programmes and set deficit-reduction goals that many politicians and analysts are sceptical Bush can meet.  \par \par \uc2 The release is not expected to have much impact on the markets other than serving as a reminder of the vast U.S. budget deficit which is one of the key drivers of dollar weakness.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040202e022001ci\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
