\par\par \b \uc2 TOCOM rubber easier in light trade.  \b0\par\par\uc2 231 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2004\par 08:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 2 (Reuters) - Tokyo rubber futures slipped on Monday in extremely light trade with market direction hard to predict due to an absence of fresh incentives and an unclear outlook in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark July 2004 rubber contract on the Tokyo Commodity Exchange settled down 2.2 yen per kg at 143.5 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Other months fell by 1.0-2.1 yen.  \par \par \uc2 "It's hard to say how the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is going to move," a Tokyo broker said.  \par \par \uc2 "There are very few fresh incentives...and trading volume has been light," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was fetching 105.61/64 yen at 0630 GMT, against 105.97/6/02 yen at about the same time on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 It held above three-year lows against the yen after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's strength.  \par \par \uc2 Traders were split in their views on the outcome of the Group of Seven (G7) meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs in Florida on Friday and Saturday.  \par \par \uc2 Turnover in TOCOM rubber was estimated at a light 5,839 lots on Monday, compared to 6,974 lots on Friday and 9,152 lots on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Open interest stood at 60,257 lots as of the end of Friday, versus 60,680 lots on Thursday and 59,916 lots on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040202e02200135\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
