\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar hovers near 3-yr low -  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  suspected.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Bases   \par \uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2004\par 07:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 2 (Reuters) - The dollar held gingerly above three-year lows against the yen on Monday after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to temper its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength before the Group of Seven (G7) meeting later this week.   \par \par \uc2 But the greenback managed a small gain against the euro, extending last week's overall climb.   \par \par \uc2 The mixed performances and tight trading ranges during Asian hours reflects a market split over what the G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs will say or do about halting the dollar's broad-based decline at their Florida meeting Friday and Saturday.   \par \par \uc2 Many traders suspected the BOJ, which spent a record 7.15 trillion yen ($67.2 billion) to prop up the dollar in January, was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on Monday in the 105.60 yen area.   \par \par \uc2 "It seems that the MOF (\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 105.58 yen," said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase in Tokyo.   \par \par \uc2 "We think the MOF is conducting smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the G7 meeting. We don't think they will be around here for ever, so if there is constant pressure, they will let dollar/yen go down gradually heading into the meeting," he added.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar stood around 105.60 yen at 0626 GMT, down from around 105.75 yen late in New York on Friday and within sight of three-year lows around 105.45 yen set a week earlier.   \par \par \uc2 "(Because of the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) people will be cautious during Tokyo trading hours. But that does not mean the dollar won't come under pressure again in European and U.S. hours," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at UFJ Bank.   \par \par \uc2 The euro fell to 1.2450 down 0.20 percent from late Friday levels. The euro was 0.30 percent lower against the yen, trading near 131.50 yen   \par \par \uc2 When the G7 met last September in Dubai, a call for flexible exchange rates set the dollar reeling.   \par \par \uc2 The consensus view at the time indicated displeasure with Asian nations manipulating the value of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, especially \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and China's yuan peg, which caused much of the dollar's weakness to play out against the euro.   \par \par \uc2 Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by various European officials in recent weeks has slowed the dollar's slide, as a stronger euro has bit deep into European exporters' profit margins.   \par \par \uc2 Now with the Florida meeting imminent, one growing view is the meeting would end without agreement on any strong statement aimed at halting the dollar's decline.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the U.S. authorities appeared in no hurry to warn against the greenback's weakness, as the U.S. economy was benefitting from the cheaper dollar while U.S. shares have rallied recently, unscathed by the dwindling value of the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Others said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could come under fire, particularly from European countries.   \par \par \uc2 "There are voices in Europe that say Japan and other Asian countries should shoulder more of the burden of the dollar's adjustment," said Daisuke Uno, market analyst at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp.   \par \par \uc2 But there was also simmering speculation that the G7 heavyweights might modify their September statement, for instance by dropping their calls for more flexibility in exchange rates.   \par \par \uc2 "It's hard to bet on either side ahead of such a big event as the coming G7 meeting," said Toshihiro Azuma, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Sumitomo Trust and Banking Corp.   \par \par \uc2 The market was also awaiting a flurry of economic data later in the day, including purchasing management indices from European countries and the U.S. Institute of Supply Management's manufacturing index. (Additional reporting by Hideyuki Sano and Shinichi Kishima in Tokyo).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040202e022000vw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
