\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  suspected around Y105.60 per dlr.  \b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2004\par 03:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 2 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) was suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, buying dollars at around 105.60 yen to prevent the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening further, traders said.   \par \par \uc2  "Unnatural (dollar) bids from Japanese banks have been seen repeatedly since early trade and they are thought to be buying on behalf of the BOJ," said a senior Japanese trader.   \par \par \uc2  Trade was fairly thin, with the dollar said to be under some selling pressure but holding around a session low near 105.60 yen, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rumoured to be lining up buy orders between 105.50 and 105.55 yen the trader said.   \par \par \uc2  The BOJ acts as the agent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF). MOF officials were not immediately available for comment.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar is hovering just above a three-year low against the yen despite repeated official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities, anxious to stop a firm yen from hurting an export-led recovery in the economy.   \par \par \uc2  Official data on Friday showed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had conducted a record volume of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January.   \par \par \uc2  The ministry data showed \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent 7.1545 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - equivalent to $67.68 billion at Monday's rate.   \par \par \uc2  That total, which covers the period between December 27 and January 28, compares with the previous monthly record of 4.4573 trillion yen last September. The Japanese authorities spent an annual record of 20 trillion in 2003.   \par \par \uc2  Most recently, the BOJ was suspected of having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Wednesday, when the dollar shot up to 106.65 yen from about 105.80 yen, traders said.   \par \par \uc2  Japanese exporters remain eager to sell the dollar to convert their proceeds into yen, particularly above 105 yen, they added.   \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the dollar's fall to pick up speed should it break below a three-year low of 105.45 yen set last week.   \par \par \uc2  As of 0226 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 105.59/63 yen compared with Friday's late U.S. level of 105.71/79. ($1=105.70 Yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040202e022000fm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
