\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  lower house approves extra  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  cash.  \b0\par\par\uc2 190 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2004\par 01:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lower house agreed to an extra budget for the current fiscal year early on Saturday, including a measure that will give authorities more ammunition to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The lower house agreed to a supplementary budget drafted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  which raises the borrowing ceiling for its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  special account, through the issuance of finance bills, to 100 trillion yen ($944 billion) from 79 trillion yen.  \par \par \uc2 The ceiling is set to be raised even higher, to 140 trillion yen, in the next fiscal year from April when parliament adopts the next annual budget.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted a record 20 trillion yen of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year to fight the yen's surge against the dollar and started 2004 in the same way with 7.1545 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January, a record for a single month.  \par \par \uc2 No new government bonds will be issued to finance the extra budget. The extra budget be formally adopted after the Upper House passes the bill some time in February. ($1=105.88 Yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040131e01v002xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
