\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Settles Lower After Release of U.S. GDP Data  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Tom Barkley  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 486 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2004\par 22:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK -- The dollar gave back some of its recent gains Friday following the release of weaker-than-expected fourth-quarter U.S. economic-growth data.  \par \par \uc2 Gross domestic product rose 4.0% in the quarter, a slowdown from the 8.2% pace in the third quarter. Economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires and CNBC had forecast a 4.8% increase.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar, which had been rallying in the wake of Wednesday's decision by Federal Reserve policy makers to drop the phrase that monetary policy will remain accommodative for a "considerable period," turned sharply lower following the data.  \par \par \uc2 The GDP figures reinforced expectations that despite the Fed's change in semantics, interest rates would likely remain at very low levels until well into the year.  \par \par \uc2 More positive U.S. data released later in the morning helped the dollar recoup some of its losses, but the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended weaker in a volatile session.  \par \par \uc2 The University of Michigan's consumer-sentiment index improved to a better-than-expected 103.8 reading at the end of January, compared with 92.6 the month before, according to those who had seen the report, which is released only to subscribers.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Purchasing Management Association of Chicago's index of area business activity rose to its highest level since July 1994 in January, at 65.9 on a seasonally adjusted basis from a revised 61.2 in December.  \par \par \uc2 However, late Friday afternoon the euro was trading higher at $1.2474, versus $1.2410 late Thursday, and also rose to 131.95 yen from 131.48 yen. Against the Swiss franc, the dollar fell to 1.2572 Swiss francs from 1.2595 francs, while sterling rose to $1.8246 from $1.8160.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar remained under pressure against the yen, following a report from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  showing that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a record 7.15 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past month.  \par \par \uc2 That was more than a third of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's total 20.1 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  during all of 2003, indicating the difficulty the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had in keeping the yen from appreciating too quickly and threatening the country's export-led recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Friday afternoon, the dollar was at 105.76 yen, down a bit from 105.95 yen late Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Tom Barkley, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4385  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     tom.barkley@dowjones.com \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Corrected Feb. 2, 2004 9:26 ET (14:26 GMT)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, the dollar remained under pressure against the yen, following a report from Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showing that the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold a record 7.15 trillion yen in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the past month.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (In the closing dollar item published Jan. 30, 2004, at 16:43 EST, the amount of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was misstated.)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020040130e01u00014\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
