\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Sold Y7.155 Tln In January  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2004\par 11:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government spent Y7.155 trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in January, as it struggled to keep the yen from rising too sharply, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data released Friday show.  \par \par \uc2 The amount for January was a record for a single month, far outstripping the previous monthly record of Y5.112 trillion set in September. It also comes on the heels of a record Y20.057 spent during 2003, which was almost triple the last annual record amount of Y7.64 trillion in 1999.  \par \par \uc2 The sheer force of Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows just how determined the government is to keep a strong yen from undermining exports, one of the main drivers of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current economic recovery. But despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar continues to slump as investors sell the greenback amid concerns over the U.S. twin current account and budget deficits and fears over possible global terrorism attacks.  \par \par \uc2 Late Friday, the dollar was trading around Y105.74, compared with around Y107.48 at the start of the year.  \par \par \uc2 To help finance January's unprecedented monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the government sold Y5.014 trillion worth of its U.S. Treasury holdings to the Bank of Japan under repurchase agreements, the ministry said.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ agreed last month it would buy up to Y10 trillion in Treasurys from the government if needed to tide the Finance Ministry over while it awaits Parliament approval for additional funding.  \par \par \uc2 The government has taken steps to raise its Y79 trillion funding limit for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Y21 trillion to Y100 trillion through an extra budget for the current fiscal year ending in March. Parliament is still debating the budget, but the bill looks set to be enacted as early as next week.  \par \par \uc2 The government will then raise the limit to Y140 trillion next fiscal year.  \par \par \uc2 The January figure was for Dec. 27 through Jan. 28 and doesn't include the last two business days of the month, for which settlements are made in the following month.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by John Gibson  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040130e01u000f1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
