\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Jan  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Data At 1000 GMT  \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2004\par 07:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 In addition to the U.S. GDP data, Tokyo players await the Japanese Finance Ministry's announcement at 1000 GMT of how much the government spent on yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders estimate the ministry spent more than Y7 trillion, which would far outstrip the previous record of Y4.46 trillion in September. It would also underscore Tokyo's unwavering determination to prevent yen gains from harming exporters, which are still fueling the economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Along with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amount, the Finance Ministry will announce how much stopgap funding it procured from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January to help finance \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It will do so by releasing the total value of U.S. Treasurys sold to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  under repurchase agreements.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ agreed last month to buy up to Y10 trillion in U.S. Treasurys when needed to help tide the government over while it waits for Parliament approval on new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funding. Analysts speculate that the BOJ has already bought some Y5 trillion worth of Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 But with Parliament expected to clear an extra budget bill for the current fiscal year as early as next week, the government is unlikely to face any serious \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funding shortages. The enactment of the extra budget will give the ministry some Y21 trillion more in funds to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with.  \par \par \uc2 Later in the Asian session, the euro took a slight tumble on position adjustments caused by lingering uncertainty over how top Group of Seven finance officials will address the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at their meeting Feb. 6-7 in the U.S.  \par \par \uc2 The euro fell below $1.2400 to near $1.2380, while also tumbling to a low of Y131.25 against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "It's a bit scary" buying euros now, said a trader at a Japanese brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040130e01u00076\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
